<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:10:58Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Macron visits Malaysia as France seeks closer defence and rare earths ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0379206122a105360f932b2f6b5d34f936a667b256fed34341db3f089e17f7e</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:10:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T03:40:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261117-macron-malaysia-france-defence-rare-earths-trade-energy--223d268813bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261117-macron-malaysia-france-defence-rare-earths-trade-energy" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron will meet Malaysian Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim in Kuala Lumpur on Tuesday to discuss strengthening defence, trade, energy and critical minerals co-operation. Macron's two-day visit, his first since 2017, comes ahead of the countries' 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations, with both sides seeking a strategic partnership.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Trump heads to Asia for historic nuclear talks with China and Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79ca1babaf29d1ef6c0780781260a176b0144d9b4a527efd40c2ed02f04b7504</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:10:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T03:07:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261117-trump-asia-nuclear-talks-china-russia--eacedd0e2220.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261117-trump-asia-nuclear-talks-china-russia" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump headed to Asia on Monday for economic talks and a planned trilateral meeting with Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin on nuclear issues and the war in Ukraine. Trump also raised the possibility of meeting North Korean leader Kim Jong Un during his visit.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>La Francophonie 'waning in global influence': Linguistic institutions becoming 'less important'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e986a064d125356b976967a923aa3e00be594b814339a02bf25bb4de9706292f</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:10:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T22:29:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261116-la-francophonie-waning-in-global-influence-linguistic-institutions-becoming-less-important--12f156dde70a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261116-la-francophonie-waning-in-global-influence-linguistic-institutions-becoming-less-important" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Phil Clark, professor of international politics at SOAS University of London. The diplomatic crisis between Rwanda and the Democratic Republic of Congo spilling out at the Francophonie summit in Phnom Penh for all to see has exposed an unexpected shift in their relations. Clark says that "nobody expected Rwanda to back down in this way" following President Macron's request that Paul Kagame withdraw Louise Mushikiwabo's candidacy for a third term.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Iran blocks UN nuclear site visits until war ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fccf4201483b3d4e44ba69d917e49bc9130aef1c7e6fa677ba69872f5be007d3</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T13:46:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261116-iran-blocks-un-nuclear-site-visits-until-war-ends--181a87828acf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261116-iran-blocks-un-nuclear-site-visits-until-war-ends" /><summary type="html">Iran's foreign ministry on Monday said that it would block the International Atomic Energy Agency's access to its damaged nuclear facilities until stated conditions for permanently ending the war have been met by the US. The ministry's statement follows calls for the UN watchdog to resume inspections of nuclear sites, which have been suspended since last year's 12-day war with Israel.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Xi, Trump and Putin to discuss 'world peace' at Shenzhen summit, China says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48cd645cbb2f63a29d1881e2f74bb4a77c90057cd1f6a213b0e42c995eff9af4</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T08:40:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261116-xi-trump-putin-discuss-world-peace-shenzhen-summit-china-says--0eb8c569a4cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261116-xi-trump-putin-discuss-world-peace-shenzhen-summit-china-says" /><summary type="html">The Chinese foreign ministry said Monday that President Xi Jinping and his US and Russian counterparts Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin would discuss "safeguarding world peace" at their first trilateral summit in Shenzhen this week. Contradicting previous official communication, Trump said he planned to add Ukraine to the agenda.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>The Philippines and Australia strengthen joint military deterrence at ASEAN summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fe220c9cb356cb7ba3ae5afc9aa1f75d10dbb9d9311adc927c142572637d83b</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T12:18:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/the-philippines-and-australia-strengthen-joint-military-deterrence-at-asean-summit--c08df64c21da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/the-philippines-and-australia-strengthen-joint-military-deterrence-at-asean-summit" /><summary type="html">Southeast Asian leaders opened their annual summit in the Philippine capital Manila on Sunday. During three days, world leaders are expected to focus on trade, energy and conflict – including the war in Iran. Donald Trump is expected to land in Manila on Tuesday. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Bangkok Tommy Walker.</summary></entry><entry><title>Philippine star Carmelle wins first Asian edition of Eurovision song contest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4605a652e71a36e78084afaccd84c8abdaada1414e64295f25c2cdc4db7f08d</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T10:26:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/philippine-star-carmelle-wins-first-asian-edition-of-eurovision-song-contest--7050e4e4ce01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/philippine-star-carmelle-wins-first-asian-edition-of-eurovision-song-contest" /><summary type="html">The Philippines has won the first Asian edition of the Eurovision Song Contest. The Filipino singer beat ten other acts to take the title in Bangkok, with a song celebrating women's empowerment. A taste of the winning song with Jack Pownall.</summary></entry><entry><title>France and Cambodia share their love for pétanque in Phnom Penh</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b937b37e58c463c90efc450e2ff47e9e49aef0b9c6d3cd17526e2fbaa72251f3</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T17:23:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261114-france-and-cambodia-share-their-love-for-p_tanque-in-phnom-penh--035fb864e2c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261114-france-and-cambodia-share-their-love-for-p%C3%A9tanque-in-phnom-penh" /><summary type="html">Phnom Penh is hosting the 20th Francophonie Summit this Sunday and Monday. French President Emmanuel Macron is attending as part of a 3-day state visit to Cambodia. France and Cambodia's history is deep rooted and complex, but the two countries have one thing in common: a love for pétanque. Story by Caitlin Brown.</summary></entry><entry><title>China to host first-ever trilateral meeting between Trump, Xi and Putin next week</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9dc275b9549ff5b92196d7af986bdbecb123c8ec6de0882440a9ac35679a1a9f</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T05:09:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261114-china-to-host-first-ever-trilateral-meeting-between-trump-xi-and-putin-next-week-us-says--a3483041e474.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261114-china-to-host-first-ever-trilateral-meeting-between-trump-xi-and-putin-next-week-us-says" /><summary type="html">The three leaders are scheduled to meet on the sidelines of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation summit in Shenzhen on Thursday, the White House confirmed. US officials said discussions will include nuclear weapons and the war in Iran, but that the war in Ukraine is unlikely to be on the agenda. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky warned the talks could prove a Yalta-like "redistribution of spheres of influence".</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>What we know about China's military exercises around Taiwan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a10bfa00434c276eb15dc182b40e6f330641a000fd498091fa4e41dab2465a4b</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T18:19:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261113-chinese-army-military-exercises-taiwan--5fe8dc54e260.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261113-chinese-army-military-exercises-taiwan" /><summary type="html">China has been carrying out major military drills around Taiwan since early November. But contrary to some claims on social media, Beijing's armed forces have not actually implemented a blockade on the island; they just simulated it.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Crossing Afghanistan along the 'highway of death'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c966d818c23f8cb8145ed4c45721726c31cab8947ba3939f4e7c3472a780cae1</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:47:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261113-crossing-afghanistan-along-the-highway-of-death--fa8fa1756aea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261113-crossing-afghanistan-along-the-highway-of-death" /><summary type="html">Highway 1, or the Ring Road, connects Afghanistan's major cities. After September 11, 2001, it became a hotspot for crime and fighting, particularly between the capital Kabul and Kandahar, the Taliban's birthplace. People taking it had to navigate extortions, kidnappings and suicide bombings. What has become of the road after the US-led war and five years of Taliban rule? Our former Afghanistan correspondent Claire Billet and photojournalist Sandra Calligaro returned to the country to find out.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar: Junta carries out double-tap airstrikes targeting civilians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cacac40efd4e9b95e295353b437a984fa821866a956bda8820903e97968b9eb1</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:41:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261113-myanmar-junta-airstrikes-civilians--249ccb264ea4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261113-myanmar-junta-airstrikes-civilians" /><summary type="html">Numerous civilian casualties have been documented in Rakhine State amid a renewed military offensive by the junta to regain control of the area.  Available evidence suggests that military aircraft are deliberately targeting civilian sites and carrying out double-tap strikes.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>El Niño fuels climate disasters: The high price of inaction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5297f49a41093868d0c1fc7d04aad1a182f02c60631dbf28d5a2821dcd23325</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:35:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261113-el-ni_o-fuels-climate-disasters-the-high-price-of-inaction--5caf5eedf5ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261113-el-ni%C3%B1o-fuels-climate-disasters-the-high-price-of-inaction" /><summary type="html">2026 is set to be one of the hottest years on record, with El Niño worsening the impact of extreme weather events. With COP31 underway in Turkey, FRANCE 24 speaks with the UNDP's climate boss about the cost of waiting in a warmer world, and with one of the student activists from Pacific Island nations who took their climate fight to the UN's highest court, and won.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>China accuses US of 'fabricating' Nvidia spy claims to push tech 'blockade'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9ed4c723e7c012794b641ec957fb3de1bc8d1a6084ba44e3da998201d504688</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T09:40:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261112-china-accuses-us-fabricating-nvidia-spy-claims-to-push-tech-blockade--374197346e02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261112-china-accuses-us-fabricating-nvidia-spy-claims-to-push-tech-blockade" /><summary type="html">China on Thursday accused the United States of “fabricating spy narratives” to justify a technology “blockade”, stepping up its pushback against reports that the woman Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang had an affair with was a Chinese intelligence asset.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Undone by a honey trap? Nvidia's Jensen Huang at heart of China spy scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fec7c6a190c76c76fd447036fa28642fcceeb6e2bfbf4f6209f544fecaf9443c</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:32:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261111-undone-by-a-honey-trap-nvidia-s-jensen-huang-at-heart-of-china-spy-scandal--ef71664cdb96.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261111-undone-by-a-honey-trap-nvidia-s-jensen-huang-at-heart-of-china-spy-scandal" /><summary type="html">It turns out that the new masters of the universe are human – all too human. Nvidia co-founder Jensen Huang has admitted to an extramarital affair with Singapore-based Chinese tech CEO Alice Huang, who is no relation. She's under scrutiny over the purchase of Nvidia state-of-the-art chips that may have been smuggled back to the mainland illegally.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>AI, affair and espionage: Why is Nvidia's chief Jensen Huang under scrutiny?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0cdedd8511e1404e6591dd1878b2840a617ce44123d0e74826f6c55ec5ae8b8</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T11:45:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-ai-affair-and-espionage-why-is-nvidia-s-chief-jensen-huang-under-scrutiny--001bc358f99a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-ai-affair-and-espionage-why-is-nvidia-s-chief-jensen-huang-under-scrutiny" /><summary type="html">Nvidia chief and tech titan Jensen Huang was in the spotlight on Monday after acknowledging an affair with a woman US officials say was working for Chinese intelligence, a claim Beijing denied.</summary></entry><entry><title>Diwali: Over one billion people mark victory of light over darkness</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec49080f00f5d9798f0576f02579c41d4317783f3d3b07b65d1947ff098bcae3</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T10:46:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/diwali-over-one-billion-people-mark-victory-of-light-over-darkness--093adc3e4b15.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/diwali-over-one-billion-people-mark-victory-of-light-over-darkness" /><summary type="html">Diwali celebrations began on Sunday, with people across India and the global diaspora gathering to mark one of the most important festivals in the Hindu tradition. In Ayodhya, believed to be the birthplace of Lord Rama, the deity celebrated during the festival, festivities included performances based on the Hindu epic Ramayana, laser and light shows, live music, fireworks and drone displays.</summary></entry><entry><title>New Zealand's knife-edge parliamentary election delivers no clear winner</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:673ee61c0f0bcaaa93f6f581ddc7180d21353fd908851e8e2c2d4babb3b018d0</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T03:01:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261108-new-zealand-election-produces-no-clear-winner-as-smaller-parties-make-record-gains--fa314d7e4925.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261108-new-zealand-election-produces-no-clear-winner-as-smaller-parties-make-record-gains" /><summary type="html">No clear winner was produced in New Zealand’s legislative elections Saturday, setting up the two main blocs – Prime Minister Christopher Luxon's right-wing coalition and opposition leader Chris Hipkins' left-wing alliance – for weeks of political wrangling to attempt to cobble together a majority. Hipkins said that while New Zealanders had spoken, "it may take us a little bit longer to figure out exactly what it is that you've said".</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>China keeps a close eye on US midterm shake-up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f0d5f4200443b7c67768c4aed025985de2f4db2cf96d81eb0def9429872b9d2</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T15:03:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261106-china-keeps-a-close-eye-on-us-midterm-shake-up--c2e2aac53d76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261106-china-keeps-a-close-eye-on-us-midterm-shake-up" /><summary type="html">The US midterm elections have resulted in the Democratic Party taking control of both chambers of the US Congress, leaving Donald Trump as a lame duck president for the remainder of his term. Professor Steve Tsang of the SOAS China Institute tells FRANCE 24 that, while a weakened Trump could strengthen Beijing's negotiating position, the Chinese leadership is aware that Congress has relatively little sway over foreign policy and is keen to maintain warm personal ties between the two presidents.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>Pollution, shortages, crime: Daily life in Pakistan's megacity Karachi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18fccd1a3eac7b12fa4a307a8aaf383ebf21ba076c9ceff0032e30720dcabc54</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T10:32:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261106-pollution-shortages-crime-daily-life-in-pakistan-s-megacity-karachi--fe424575ae00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261106-pollution-shortages-crime-daily-life-in-pakistan-s-megacity-karachi" /><summary type="html">Fed up with hours of power cuts, the residents of Pakistan's economic hub Karachi took to the streets in recent days and blocked several major roads. The outburst of anger highlights the daily problems faced by a megacity of over 21 million people, which has once again been ranked among the world's least liveable cities.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar: Civilians under fire from military junta</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2788ca514ccb9c70f17467712eebedddedeb8e5c3c4ab470e71f579257d4598b</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T17:58:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-myanmar-civilians-under-fire-from-military-junta--4174803e3ee2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-myanmar-civilians-under-fire-from-military-junta" /><summary type="html">More than five years after the military coup, the junta launched a new offensive in September to retake Rakhine State, intensifying airstrikes against civilians and employing double-tap strikes.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong activist jailed for 10 more years for collusion with foreign forces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd924a175261f7bea7615e4283527028b11aacb816fc5589758536028930f3e6</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:29:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-hong-kong-activist-jailed-for-10-more-years-for-collusion-with-foreign-forces--7a7e3bb3e8a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-hong-kong-activist-jailed-for-10-more-years-for-collusion-with-foreign-forces" /><summary type="html">Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong was sentenced to 10 more years in jail on Thursday for colluding with foreign powers, the second time he has been penalised under the city's national security law. Hong, 30, is one of the most globally recognised faces of Hong Kong's pro-democracy movement and has already spent almost six years behind bars. He is now not due for release until late 2036.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong activist Joshua Wong gets 10 more years in jail for foreign collusion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b6cc7a5ea2fa4db5e311bdb6ada920f7d6997c70b5d86c8d644149c08ab8445</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T03:31:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-joshua-wong-hong-kong-10-years-jail-foreign-collusion--961948348fab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-joshua-wong-hong-kong-10-years-jail-foreign-collusion" /><summary type="html">Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong was sentenced to 10 more years in prison on Thursday for colluding with foreign powers, a court summary said. Wong, 30, pleaded guilty in September to seeking foreign sanctions against Hong Kong and China under Beijing’s national security law, having spent nearly six years imprisoned.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea to deploy military mission to keep Strait of Hormuz open</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c680873f5b5faa8505f259921fe4bddd401dc17eb28a781eadbfaee3778c02c</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T02:17:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-south-korea-military-mission-strait-of-hormuz--37e442fe8805.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-south-korea-military-mission-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">South Korea will deploy maritime patrol aircraft and an explosive ordnance disposal team near the Strait of Hormuz to help keep the waterway open, its defence ministry said Thursday. Seoul said it would protect commercial shipping and energy supplies while ruling out military intervention in the ongoing US-Iran war.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>How Chinese AI is censoring the controversy around Mbappé’s Chairman Mao comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89e120253047f248b6bfe4c5a94b005bba9d9db22bf4e694361a0cdf4f6a0eac</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T20:28:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261104-how-chinese-ai-is-censoring-the-controversy-around-mbappes-chairman-mao-comments--925db7d6d62f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261104-how-chinese-ai-is-censoring-the-controversy-around-mbappes-chairman-mao-comments" /><summary type="html">Footballer Kylian Mbappé sparked a wave of condemnation across China when he implied that Chinese leader Mao Zedong was a dictator. In China, information about this controversy is being censored by Chinese AI chatbots.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea pushes digital detox for young people addicted to screens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b213756683e2618f0ac05a4393f924fe07bed33c29f6a7b0185456af47c4c2d3</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:14:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261104-south-korea-pushes-digital-detox-for-young-people-addicted-to-screens--7a9ca277cb2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261104-south-korea-pushes-digital-detox-for-young-people-addicted-to-screens" /><summary type="html">Back in August, France's Constitutional Council overturned a social media ban for children under 15. Some students, though, are now banned from using their smartphones at school. In South Korea, where an estimated 40 percent of young children and teens are addicted to their mobile devices, authorities are trying to find ways to drastically reduce their screen time – a huge challenge in such a hyper-connected society. FRANCE 24's Chloé Borgnon, Aruna Popuri and Justin McCurry report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea rejects US allegations over $6 billion Binance crypto heist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f380a835a343dbb7d08b2e454975c33cb0ff9ceb040b253cb89cdaeeb9886175</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T23:49:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261102-north-korea-rejects-us-allegations-over-6-billion-binance-crypto-heist--685d3b1c8c8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261102-north-korea-rejects-us-allegations-over-6-billion-binance-crypto-heist" /><summary type="html">North Korea on Tuesday dismissed US allegations that it was behind a $6 billion cryptocurrency theft from Binance as "absurd rhetoric", accusing Washington of seeking to portray the country as a cybercriminal state and warning that US hostility could affect future diplomatic engagement.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Football: China refuses to air Real Madrid game after Mbappé comment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d6ee70b85679b07e35eecc290608210a612f7385e4d71048720b06058b51f1c</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T11:09:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-football-china-refuses-to-air-real-madrid-game-after-mbapp_-comment--ab89cdb57c26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-football-china-refuses-to-air-real-madrid-game-after-mbapp%C3%A9-comment" /><summary type="html">Chinese state broadcaster CCTV did not broadcast a Real Madrid La Liga match on Sunday after star forward Kylian Mbappé caused a furore in China with remarks he made about former leader Mao Zedong. FRANCE 24's correspondent Jan Camenzind Broomby reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Taliban voices 'serious concern' over US plan to deport Afghan migrants via Pakistan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:379bb041e8f531c7501ac69ab2348ff6df351835ca10df40f9d19223c0d97eea</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T07:26:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261102-taliban-voice-alarm-over-us-plan-to-deport-afghan-migrants-via-pakistan--7e5b3b112799.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261102-taliban-voice-alarm-over-us-plan-to-deport-afghan-migrants-via-pakistan" /><summary type="html">Afghanistan's Taliban government expressed concern on Monday over reported US plans to deport more than 150 Afghans from the US to Pakistan for an eventual return home, with advocacy groups warning the removal could endanger their lives.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands join Indian opposition protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57da87b58fec04bcb98abc41ce142610082b75e9be529c444448949751035d1b</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T17:45:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/thousands-join-indian-opposition-protest--b6cc09af60fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-join-indian-opposition-protest" /><summary type="html">India’s opposition parties staged major protests in New Delhi on Sunday against Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s government and a nationwide voter list review that has fuelled demonstrations since the summer, led by the youth movement Cockroach Janta Party. Eliza Herbert reports.</summary></entry></feed>
